questions.explanation:
**Given:**

Two complementary angles, difference in measures = 22&deg;.

**Formula Used:**

Sum of complementary angles = 90&deg;

**Calculation:**

&rArr; Let the smaller angle be x.

&rArr; Bigger angle = x + 22&deg;

&rArr; x + (x + 22&deg;) = 90&deg;

&rArr; 2x + 22&deg; = 90&deg;

&rArr; 2x = 90&deg; - 22&deg;

&rArr; 2x = 68&deg;

&rArr; x = 68&deg; &divide; 2

&rArr; x = 34&deg;

&rArr; Bigger angle = x + 22&deg;

&rArr; Bigger angle = 34&deg; + 22&deg;

&rArr; Bigger angle = 56&deg;

**&there4; The correct answer is 56&deg;.**

